  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "A leap toward the medal race",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "rellik13 has climbed from 265th at the previous close to 28th, adding 4.75 points to reach 36.55. That is a substantial advance through a crowded field, but it leaves the entry 1.43 points below the provisional gold score of 37.98. goonew has also made ground, rising from 229th to 39th with a 3.86-point gain. Neither move changes the contest’s leading order."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The leaders keep their distance",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-dries-smit-roster-1"
      ],
      "text": "Tufa Labs holds first at 68.91, with Yi-Chia Chen second at 67.49: the gap remains 1.42 points. Dries Smit remains in Tufa’s observed roster. Team Turducken stays third at 52.82 ahead of mtg and the last dance. NVARC3 remains tenth at 43.94. The unchanged top ten puts the day’s sharpest movement further down the board; a big climb there still has to cross the gold line before it challenges the leading group."
    },
    {
      "heading": "One result needs a second look",
      "sourceIds": [
        "discussion-arc-3-750981",
        "discussion-arc-3-750885"
      ],
      "text": "Two public discussions offer a useful caution for the chase. Lavin Wins reports that an identical notebook version fell from 32.76 to 24.03 and asks whether scoring conditions changed; the thread has no organizer answer. Separately, Francise Liang reports variation between unchanged public-game tests of Daniel Franzen’s Milestone 2 notebook and recommends repeated comparisons. Liang’s experiments with more concurrent games and an earlier stall cutoff scored worse in those tests. These are participant reports, not a confirmed infrastructure change or proof of hidden-game performance."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The morning jump in perspective",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-20-0602-arc-3-wkdrbwnd1-jumps-to-twenty-sixth"
      ],
      "text": "The wire’s morning report recorded wkdrbwnd1 reaching 26th at 36.77. That remains useful context for the depth of the chase, rather than evidence of a second gain this evening. With the leaders unchanged, the immediate sporting question is which of the rising challengers can turn a large rank jump into a score above the provisional gold line."
    }
